config XIAOMI_METIS
	tristate "Xiaomi METIS policy layer (6.18 aligned)"
	depends on ARM64 && ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS && ANDROID_VENDOR_OEM_DATA
	default n
	help
	  Xiaomi METIS task policy for rodin: VIP/lock-inheritance marking,
	  cold-start protection, cluster affinity and frequency boost, all
	  attached to native GKI vendor hooks. The stock pick-side scheduler
	  (private rbtree/pick/preempt ladder/deadline tree), WALT remnants,
	  private load balancer and EAS replication are dropped: 6.18 owns
	  the scheduling core, load tracking, uclamp and energy-aware
	  placement; this layer keeps only SoC/task policy on live hooks.
	  Carrier state lives in the mi_schedule task slots. All exported
	  symbols have in-tree consumers; no closed-scheduler ABI stubs.
